# Patch: accept real-world keybox private keys and ECDSA curve/hash combos
#
# Upstream: Enginex0/tricky-addon-enhanced @ v5.53.1 (5c5e497)
# Applies to: rust/src/keybox/validate.rs
#
# Fixes two validator false-negatives that make every common keybox fail the
# fetch-time validation ("private key present but unparseable" /
# "chain verification failed: hop 0 -> 1"):
#   1. Private keys are now decoded from PEM to DER by the validator itself
#      before handing them to RustCrypto. Real keyboxes ship SEC1
#      ("BEGIN EC PRIVATE KEY") keys and/or single-line, >64-column base64
#      bodies that the strict RustCrypto PEM readers reject.
#   2. ECDSA verification now supports curve/hash combinations ring does not
#      provide, e.g. an ecdsa-with-SHA256 certificate signed by a P-384
#      issuer (via the p256/p384 crates' prehash verifiers).
#
# Both defects were verified against the Yurikey keybox and a working
# device keybox: chains and keys verify with OpenSSL but were rejected by
# the unpatched validator.
